<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates generally steady.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates generally steady.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were generally unchanged ahead of the weekly Treasury bills auction during which many expected rates to move sideways, traders said.</p>
<p>Fresh inflow from maturing bills are expected to add liquidity to the system which was affected by the Central Bank's selling of dollars, they said.</p>
<p>Only two-week and one-month money slipped, both falling to 11.25 percent from 11.3125 percent.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  OCT 28		 OCT 25</p>
<p>    1 W		11  1/4		11  1/4</p>
<p>    2 W		11  1/4		11  5/16</p>
<p>    1 M		11  1/4		11  5/16</p>
<p>    2 M		11  5/16	     11  5/16</p>
<p>    3 M		11  7/16	     11  7/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11 11/16	     11 11/16</p>
<p>    12M		11 13/16	     11 13/16</p>
<p>    VAL		29-Oct		  28-Oct</p>
